liable signals combine  that with the internet of things and the  possibilities are limitless iot is a  term used for anything that takes the  internet beyond our computers iot will  be the keystone technology for  futuristic settings such as smart cities  robot driven agriculture and  self-driving highway systems and 5g is  expected to be the connectivity backbone  of that future one of the biggest  bottlenecks of the current iot system is  bandwidth and latency a 5g network  solves both the problems so with proper  implementation iot has the potential to  flourish once 5g becomes ubiquitous  allowing us to live in a totally  connected world where physical and  digital systems are seamlessly  integrated with the internet satellite  constellations a few years ago elon musk  spacex launched the first batch of 60  satellites as part of their starlink  project today there is a constellation  of over 2 000 satellites already up in  the low earth orbit with a plan of  inserting 40 to 50 000 more in the  coming years this may sound like a crazy  idea but it's not without its merits  currently the internet travels through  undersea optical fiber cables that  criss-cross the world's oceans and you  can find out more about that in this  video i did about it unfortunately this  leads to many transmission  inefficiencies as delivery is reliant on  physical wires this is also why it is  impossible to provide every square inch  of the planet with internet connectivity  there are various spots on the earth  currently where you cannot get internet  access satellite constellations are an  ideal solution to these two problems  imagine a giant canopy of satellites  covering the entirety of earth beaming  down the internet even in the remotest  of places this universal access to the  internet will have profound effects on  our society especially in the developing  world as information becomes readily  available  self-healing concrete  shifting to the world of construction  self-healin